<article class="env-lemma" id="0C34">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C34">Lemma <span data-tag="0C34">15.39.3</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $(A, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a complete local $k$-algebra. If $\kappa /k$ is separable, then there exists a $k$-algebra map $\kappa \to A$ such that $\kappa \to A \to \kappa $ is $\text{id}_\kappa $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/0322" data-tag="0322">10.158.9</a> the extension $\kappa /k$ is formally smooth. By Lemma <a href="/tag/07EC" data-tag="07EC">15.38.2</a> $k \to \kappa $ is formally smooth in the sense of Definition <a href="/tag/07EB" data-tag="07EB">15.38.1</a>. Then we get $\kappa \to A$ from Lemma <a href="/tag/07NJ" data-tag="07NJ">15.38.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>